/* test-no-warnings */
// Issue #1171: cross-file modification tracking was gated on cppDetected, so
// in C mode a parameter that is only ever forwarded to a cross-file *mutating*
// callee still received #268 auto-const.
//
// `s` is never written locally, so PassByValueAnalyzer saw no local write and
// applied auto-const, emitting `const Sample*`. Sensors.bump does mutate its
// parameter, so lib/sensors.h declares `Sample*` — and the call discarded the
// const qualifier:
//
//     warning: passing argument 1 of 'Sensors__bump' discards 'const'
//              qualifier from pointer target type [-Wdiscarded-qualifiers]
//
// The transpiler still exited 0. C++ mode was already correct (`Sample&` on
// both sides), so the divergence was C-mode-only: one decision — "does this
// callee modify its parameter?" — was answered from accumulated cross-file
// data in C++ and from per-file data only in C.
//
// This fixture is test-no-warnings rather than test-execution because
// execution fixtures compile without warning flags; only validateNoWarnings
// uses -Wall -Wextra -Werror, which is what turns the discarded qualifier
// into a failure.
#include "lib/sensors.cnx"

scope Consumer {
    // Forwards `s` to a mutating cross-file callee and never writes it
    // locally. Must NOT get auto-const.
    public void bumpTwice(Sample s) {
        Sensors.bump(s);
        Sensors.bump(s);
    }

    // Forwards `s` to a non-mutating cross-file callee. Auto-const must still
    // apply, so the fix cannot be "withhold const whenever the callee is in
    // another file".
    public u8 readTwice(Sample s) {
        u8 first <- Sensors.readValue(s);
        u8 second <- Sensors.readValue(s);
        return first + second;
    }
}
